    "created_at": "2016-08-17T16:50:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T16:50:16Z",
    "body": "I don't see it in chromium's or gecko's default styles, FWIW. But also the initial value of `hyphens` is `manual` and there is no default style in HTML to override that, so developers already need to opt-in to enabling hyphens with `hyphens: auto`.\n\nNote that `hyphens: none` disables `&shy;`, it's not clear to me that makes sense as a default style.\n\nI think it could make sense to add `code { hyphens: manual }` (not sure about `kbd` and `samp`) to HTML if the initial value of `hyphens` is changed from `manual` to `auto` in CSS.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
