    "created_at": "2016-08-26T20:23:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-26T20:23:52Z",
    "body": "I think it would be a good addition to the default styles, because when authors enable hyphens they often don't remember to turn them off for such things, and it is a reasonable default to have it disabled within `<code>` and `<kbd>`. (It seems unlikely that someone would specifically want hyphenation to take effect inside `<code>` and `<kbd>`--I can't imagine a single case where that would be appropriate, and many where it would confuse the reader.)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
