    "created_at": "2016-08-27T09:48:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-27T10:48:18Z",
    "body": "Just wanted to make sure we're on the same page:\n- `hyphens` is implemented except [Blink](http://crbug.com/605840) for years.\n- The initial value is `manual`, not `auto`, so the automatic hyphenation is already disabled. This bug is about not to break at `&shy;` in `code`, `samp`, and `kbd`.\n\nCorrect?\n\nI don't have strong opinions either way but I can't imagine when/how/for what purposes authors use `&shy;` in `code`, `samp`, and `kbd`. Do we have some examples or data when they do, how it's useful, and this change doesn't break authors intentions?\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
